<job_description>
Research Engineer 5/6 – AI for Member Systems
USA - Remote

Job Posting Date
05-27-2026
Job Requisition ID
JR31233
Teams
Data & Insights
Work Type
Remote
At Netflix, our mission is to entertain the world. Together, we are writing the next episode - pushing the boundaries of storytelling, global fandom and making the unimaginable a reality. We are a dream team obsessed with the uncomfortable excitement of discovering what happens when you merge creativity, intuition and cutting-edge technology. Come be a part of what’s next.

As Netflix continues to grow, so do the opportunities to enhance our personalization systems and algorithms. We're looking for a passionate and talented Research Engineer to join our Al for Member Systems. In this role, you will apply your expertise in machine learning and software engineering to design, develop, and scale solutions that power the Netflix experience.

Key Responsibilities:
Collaborate with cross-functional teams, including researchers, engineers, data scientists, and product managers, to develop and implement machine learning algorithms that improve personalization, recommendations, and member experiences.

Create scalable, production-ready ML solutions, taking algorithms from initial concept through to deployment in Netflix's large-scale, real-time systems.

Optimize the performance and scalability of machine learning models, ensuring they can handle the diverse tastes and behaviors of our global member base.

Design and conduct offline experiments and A/B tests to validate the impact of algorithmic changes on key business metrics.

Contribute to the ongoing improvement of our ML infrastructure and tooling, ensuring that we stay at the cutting edge of industry practices.

Engage in continuous learning and development, staying up-to-date with the latest advances in machine learning and software engineering.

What we are looking for:
5+ years of experience in applying machine learning in an industrial setting, with a track record of delivering impactful results.

PhD or Masters in Computer Science, Statistics, or a related field

Expertise in machine learning algorithms and frameworks, with hands-on experience in training, tuning, and deploying models in production environments.

Excellent software design and development skills in Python along with Scala, Java, C++, or C#

Experience in one or more of the following applied fields: Recommendations, Personalization, Long-term Reward Modeling, Bandits, Transformers, Large-Scale Language Models, LLM evaluation, RLHF reward modeling/alignment

Great interpersonal skills including strong written and verbal communication

Preferred Qualifications:
Experience building or enhancing personalization systems, search engines, or similar large-scale machine learning applications.

Background in neural networks, natural language processing, or causal inference

Contributions to open-source projects in machine learning or related fields.

Experience working with cross functional teams

Links:
Netflix Research site

Our long term business view

NOTE: This job posting is inclusive of a variety of positions within our AI for Member Systems (AIMS) Engineering group. Based on your background, expertise and interests, we will route you to the appropriate team(s). All teams may not be hiring at the same time.

 

Generally, our compensation structure consists solely of an annual salary; we do not have bonuses. You choose each year how much of your compensation you want in salary versus stock options. To determine your personal top of market compensation, we rely on market indicators and consider your specific job family, background, skills, and experience to determine your compensation in the market range. The range for this role is $600,000.00 - $1,066,000.00. This compensation range will vary based on location.
Netflix provides comprehensive benefits including Health Plans, Mental Health support, a 401(k) Retirement Plan with employer match, Stock Option Program, Disability Programs, Health Savings and Flexible Spending Accounts, Family-forming benefits, and Life and Serious Injury Benefits. We also offer paid leave of absence programs. Full-time hourly employees accrue 35 days annually for paid time off to be used for vacation, holidays, and sick paid time off. Full-time salaried employees are immediately entitled to flexible time off. See more details about our Benefits here.

Netflix is a unique culture and environment. Learn more here.

Inclusion is a Netflix value and we strive to host a meaningful interview experience for all candidates. If you want an accommodation/adjustment for a disability or any other reason during the hiring process, please send a request to your recruiting partner.

We are an equal-opportunity employer and celebrate diversity, recognizing that diversity builds stronger teams. We approach diversity and inclusion seriously and thoughtfully. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, ancestry, national origin, caste, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, age, disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic makeup, marital status, or military service.

Job is open for no less than 7 days and will be removed when the position is filled.
</job_description>

<instructions>
Extract the information from the job description and format the result as a single valid JSON object that adheres strictly to the following schema and key requirements:

1. company_and_domain:
   - company_name (string): Name of the company. If not mentioned, return "Not specified".
   - company_domain (string): Main industry or business area. If unknown, return "Unknown".
   - business_scale (string or null): Business scale if mentioned (e.g., DAU, number of customers, data volume, request rates). Otherwise, null. Do not use nested objects/dicts here.

2. role_and_architecture:
   - seniority_level (string): Seniority level. If unknown, return "Not specified".
   - is_people_manager (boolean): Does the role involve direct people management/HR duties?
   - is_tech_leader (boolean): Does the role involve technical leadership?
   - team_name (string): Name of the specific team. If unknown, return "Not specified".
   - job_focus (string): Main focus of the job (e.g., RnD, Production, Applied ML).
   - project_name (string): Name of the product or project.
   - role_domain (string): Specific business or problem domain the role focuses on.
   - data_signals (list of strings): Specific types of data or features the role works with (e.g., user behavior, transaction history, text sentiment, real-time load).
   - operational_constraints (list of strings): Production/operational requirements and constraints (e.g., latency, throughput, high availability, drift detection, rollback mechanisms).
   - planning_horizon (string or null): Architectural or strategic timeframes (e.g., "next 18 months", "long-term roadmap"). Otherwise, null.

3. tasks_and_responsibilities (list of strings):
   - Extract tasks as an array of exact duties.
   - Ensure inclusion of end-to-end lifecycle stages (e.g., data sourcing, model design, offline/online evaluation, deployment, monitoring) and cross-functional duties (e.g., stakeholder communication, project estimation).

4. ai_and_ml_methodology_focus:
   - requires_classical_ml (boolean): Does the role require classical ML? Set to true if classical ML, statistical modeling, probabilistic models, or optimization are mentioned.
   - requires_llms (boolean): Does the role require Generative AI / LLM usage? Set to true if LLMs, GenAI, RAG, prompt engineering, or fine-tuning are mentioned.
   - requires_agentic_ai (boolean): Does the role explicitly require Agentic AI / Autonomous Agents? Set to true if explicitly contains terms like "agentic", "autonomous", "tool use", or "multi-agent".
   - extra (list of strings): List of extra AI/ML subfields or requirements (e.g., "Computer Vision", "NLP", "RecSys", "Reinforcement Learning") if mentioned. If none, return an empty array [].

5. skills_analysis:
   - Must be a dictionary containing exactly three keys: "technical_skills", "soft_skills", and "languages".
   - Each of these keys must map to a list of skill objects.
   - Each skill object in all three lists must have the exact same structure:
     - skill_name (string): Name of the skill or technology.
     - critical_level (string): How critical this skill is. Strictly one of: "Core", "Secondary", "Optional".
     - proficiency_level (string): Required candidate proficiency level. Strictly one of: "Low", "Middle", "High".
     - context (string): How the skill will be used in practice. State what the skill is used for based on the text. If inferred, write "Inferred from: [quote]".
   - Mandatorily extract programming languages, frameworks, methodologies, tools, and MLOps/DevOps concepts.
   - For soft_skills, look for business-oriented traits (e.g., Project Estimation, Trade-off analysis, Stakeholder Management).
   - For languages, parse any language requirements (e.g., English, German) and use the exact same skill object structure. If no languages are specified, return an empty list [].

6. EXCLUSIONS:
   - Ignore standard HR boilerplate, benefits, and EEO statements, unless they reveal the company domain or work model (e.g., hybrid/remote).
</instructions>

<constraints>
1. ACCURACY: Preserve the exact terminology and technical granularity of the original text. Do not generalize specific algorithms or infrastructure tools into broad categories.
2. COMPLETENESS: Do not omit system constraints, data types, or non-coding technical tasks.
3. TRACEABILITY: If a requirement is a hybrid of engineering and product (e.g., "defining ML metrics from business goals"), capture it fully with precise context.
4. STRICT JSON FORMATTING: Do not wrap the JSON object with any other tags besides markdown block. Strictly output a valid JSON object matching the requested schema. Ensure all fields are correctly named and have the correct data types.
</constraints>


