### Professional Summary
Senior Applied Scientist with 10+ years of experience building and deploying large-scale machine learning systems for personalization, recommendations, and user behavior modeling. Expertise in classical ML, deep learning, and LLMs, with a proven track record of driving business impact through A/B testing and offline experimentation. Strong engineering background in Python, PySpark, and cloud-native MLOps. Passionate about building scalable, real-time ML solutions that enhance member experiences.

### Key Achievements
- Engineered a real-time adaptive personalization system for a mobile game with millions of users, optimizing user experience and driving a 20% LTV increase and 50% churn reduction, validated through rigorous A/B testing.
- Designed and validated a churn prediction model using offline experimentation on tabular user behavior data, resulting in an estimated 20% LTV growth.
- Built a player behavior embedding model based on Mamba (SSM) architecture to capture long-term behavioral patterns, reducing player segmentation mismatches by 30%.
- Developed and deployed a scalable demand forecasting ML pipeline for global FMCG clients, improving product availability by 5% and reducing perishable waste by 7%, leveraging PySpark and Databricks.

### Professional Experience

**Principal ML Engineer** | VOKI Games (Playrix) | Sep 2025 – Present | Serbia
- Spearheaded the development of a real-time adaptive personalization system that optimized player experience, leading to 20% LTV growth and 50% churn reduction; designed and conducted A/B tests to validate algorithmic changes.
- Built a churn prediction model using classical ML (XGBoost) on tabular user behavior data, conducting offline experiments to measure impact, driving an estimated 20% LTV increase.
- Designed and implemented a user behavior embedding model using Mamba (SSM) transformers to capture long-term preferences, reducing segmentation mismatches by 30%.
- Developed a multi-agent LLM pipeline (GPT, Claude) with a custom simulation engine for automated content generation, reducing level design time by 40%.
- Collaborated with cross-functional teams (product, engineering, data) to align AI roadmap with business goals and integrate models into production.

**Head of Data Science & Analytics** | Rubbles (SBDA Group) | Jan 2023 – Aug 2025 | Serbia
- Led a team of 20 data scientists and engineers, driving the development of scalable ML solutions for demand forecasting and personalization in retail; remained hands-on in model development and deployment.
- Designed and deployed a production-ready demand forecasting toolkit using LightGBM, PySpark, and Databricks, integrated into major FMCG clients (KFC, Mars, Unilever), increasing product availability by 5%.
- Built an internal LLM-based RAG system (LangChain, FAISS) for knowledge retrieval, reducing new engineer onboarding time by 50%.
- Served as primary technical liaison to C-level executives, translating business requirements into ML roadmaps and presenting ROI-driven performance reports.

**Lead ML Engineer** | Rubbles | Apr 2022 – Jan 2023 | Turkey
- Engineered promo elasticity and demand forecasting models (LightGBM, XGBoost) for Perfetti Van Melle, reducing stock-outs by 15% and excess inventory by 10%.
- Designed and deployed production ML services using Spark and Docker, ensuring high-throughput data processing and seamless backend integration.
- Mentored a team of 5+ developers, establishing code review and testing best practices for robust ML infrastructure.

**Senior ML Engineer** | Rubbles | Nov 2021 – Apr 2022 | Russia
- Architected a global-scale demand forecasting system for a leading QSR brand, improving forecast accuracy (WAPE) by 12% through advanced feature engineering and real-time traffic signals.
- Implemented real-time features that boosted campaign ROI and reduced perishable food waste by 7%.

**Senior ML Engineer** | NDA (Leading Oil & Gas Company) | Jun 2017 – Nov 2021 | Russia
- Led the Energy Efficiency project, developing dynamic ML models and factor analysis algorithms for energy consumption, achieving 5-7% cost reduction.
- Headed the Data Science department, overseeing resource allocation across multiple IIoT projects and mentoring a team of 6+ engineers.
- Designed and deployed an automated anomaly detection system for oil production (Keras, TensorFlow), reducing equipment downtime by 12%.
- Architected a "Digital Twin for Oil Manufacture" MVP, building scalable backend services (Python, K8s, Kafka) and deploying ML models to simulate complex refining processes.

### Skills & Languages
- **Machine Learning:** Classical ML (classification, regression, forecasting), Deep Learning (Transformers, SSMs, CNNs), Recommendation & Personalization Systems, A/B Testing & Offline Experimentation, LLMs & Generative AI (RAG, prompt engineering, RLHF concepts).
- **Programming:** Python, C++, SQL.
- **Frameworks & Tools:** PyTorch, TensorFlow, Keras, LightGBM, XGBoost, Scikit-learn, Hugging Face, LangChain, FAISS, vLLM, Mamba.
- **Data & MLOps:** PySpark, Databricks, Airflow, Docker, Kubernetes, Azure, AWS, MLflow, Weights & Biases.
- **Soft Skills:** Cross-functional collaboration, technical communication, mentoring, continuous learning.
- **Languages:** English (Fluent, C1), Russian (Native).

### Education
- **2021:** PhD Candidate in Computer Science – SPbPU (ABD)
- **2017:** MSc in Technical Systems Management – SPbPU, Russia (Honors)
- **2015:** BSc in Computer Sciences – SPbPU, Russia
- **2013:** Erasmus Exchange – Czech Technical University, Prague (full program in English)

### Additional
- Open to relocation to the United States; visa sponsorship required. Willing to self-fund relocation expenses.
- [Recommendations from professionals and leaders at top-tier tech companies](https://www.linkedin.com/in/nkudriashov/details/recommendations/?detailScreenTabIndex=0)
