### Professional Summary

Senior Applied ML Engineer with 10+ years of experience designing, building, and deploying large-scale machine learning systems across personalization, recommendations, forecasting, and adaptive UX. Deep expertise in classical ML, neural networks, transformers, and large-scale language models, with a strong track record of taking algorithms from research concept to production in real-time, high-throughput environments. Proven ability to design and execute offline experiments and A/B tests, optimize model performance at scale, and collaborate cross-functionally with researchers, engineers, data scientists, and product managers. Fluent English (C1).

### Key Achievements

*   Designed and deployed **15+ production ML solutions** across personalization, recommendations, forecasting, and RAG/LLM systems — generating **>300% ROI** and reducing operational costs for major global clients (KFC, Mars, Henkel, Unilever, Perfetti Van Melle).
*   Built and shipped a **churn prediction classification model** (gradient boosting) for Match-3 games, identifying at-risk players and driving an estimated **20% LTV growth** and **50% churn reduction**.
*   Engineered a **player experience embedding model** using Mamba (SSM) architecture to capture long-term behavioral patterns, reducing player segmentation mismatches by **30%**.
*   Architected a **global-scale demand forecasting system** for a leading QSR brand, improving WAPE by **12%** through advanced feature engineering and real-time traffic signals.
*   Designed and taught a **Generative AI & ML course (30+ lectures)** at EPIC Institute of Technology, mentoring the next generation of ML practitioners.

### Professional Experience

#### VOKI Games (Playrix)
*The #1 European mobile game publisher*

**Principal ML Engineer**
Sep 2025 – Present, Serbia, Novi Sad
*   Developed a roadmap for the enterprise-wide integration of AI models across personalization, recommendations, and member experience systems.
*   Built and deployed a churn prediction classification model for Match-3 games to identify at-risk players, driving an estimated 20% LTV growth and 50% churn reduction.
*   Designed and implemented a player experience embedding model based on Mamba (SSM) architecture to capture long-term behavioral patterns, reducing player segmentation mismatches by 30%.
*   Developed a Multi-Agent GenAI framework to automate Match-3 level creation; integration with a custom gameplay simulator accelerated the level design pipeline time by 40%.

#### Rubbles (SBDA Group)
*Company specializing in data-driven business process optimization for large enterprises.*

**Head of Data Science & Analytics**
Jan 2023 – Aug 2025, Serbia, Novi Sad
*   Designed ML demand forecasting toolkit. Led integration into major FMCG clients (KFC, Mars, Henkel, Unilever), increasing product availability by 5% on average.
*   Built internal LLM-based RAG system for knowledge retrieval (LangChain, FAISS). Reduced onboarding time by 50% for new engineers.
*   Served as a primary technical liaison for the CEO and stakeholders, aligning AI roadmaps with business goals and presenting ROI-driven performance reports to C-level executives.
*   Managed a team of 20 data scientists and analysts across 5 parallel product integrations, establishing rigorous code review and unit testing standards for scalable ML infrastructure.

**Lead ML Engineer**
Apr 2022 – Jan 2023, Turkey, Istanbul
*   Engineered demand and promo elasticity models (LightGBM, XGBoost, Statsmodels) for Perfetti Van Melle, resulting in a 15% reduction in stock-outs and a 10% decrease in excess inventory.
*   Designed and deployed production-ready ML services using Spark and Docker, ensuring high-throughput data processing and seamless integration with backend infrastructure.
*   Collaborated tightly with backend engineering teams by analyzing and reviewing existing Java and Scala codebases to ensure robust deployment of ML pipelines.
*   Orchestrated cross-functional delivery and mentored a team of 5+ developers, establishing best practices for code robustness and scalable AI infrastructure.

**Senior ML Engineer**
Nov 2021 – Apr 2022, Russian Federation, Moscow
*   Architected a global-scale demand forecasting system for a leading QSR brand, improving WAPE by 12% through advanced feature engineering.
*   Directly boosted campaign ROI and product availability by implementing real-time traffic features, resulting in a 7% reduction in perishable food waste.

#### NDA (Confidential Client)
*Largest gas producer and top oil and gas company.*

**Senior ML Engineer**
Jun 2017 – Nov 2021, Russian Federation, Moscow
*   Led the Energy Efficiency & Cost Optimization project. Developed dynamic ML models and factor analysis algorithms for energy consumption. Achieved an estimated 5-7% reduction in energy costs.
*   Scaled AI Operations & Strategy: Headed the Data Science department, overseeing resource allocation across multiple IIoT projects and mentoring a cross-functional team of 6+.
*   Designed and deployed an automated anomaly detection solution for oil production (Keras, TensorFlow). Reduced equipment downtime by 12%.
*   Digital Twin Engineering: Architected a "Digital Twin for Oil Manufacture" MVP, simulating complex refining processes. Built the scalable backend (Python, K8s, Kafka) and interpreted ML models to identify dynamic properties of technological objects, accelerating R&D cycles for complex industrial assets.

