### Professional Summary

Senior Applied ML Engineer with 10+ years of experience designing and deploying data-driven solutions across industrial, retail, and energy sectors. Deep expertise in classical machine learning, time series forecasting, anomaly detection, and optimization, applied to large-scale operational KPIs. Proven track record of end-to-end ML project delivery — from problem framing and feature engineering to production deployment and stakeholder reporting. Strong theoretical foundation in probability, statistics, and optimization. Fluent English (C1).

### Key Achievements

*   Built and deployed **15+ ML solutions** in production across forecasting, anomaly detection, and optimization — generating **>300% ROI** and reducing operational costs for major enterprise clients.
*   Designed and deployed an automated anomaly detection solution for oil production (Keras, TensorFlow), reducing equipment downtime by **12%** through time series analysis.
*   Architected a global-scale demand forecasting system for a leading QSR brand, improving WAPE by **12%** through advanced feature engineering and time series modeling.
*   Engineered demand and promo elasticity models (LightGBM, XGBoost, Statsmodels), resulting in a **15% reduction in stock-outs** and a **10% decrease in excess inventory**.
*   Led the Energy Efficiency & Cost Optimization project, developing dynamic ML models and factor analysis algorithms for energy consumption, achieving an estimated **5–7% reduction in energy costs**.
*   Designed and taught Generative AI & ML course **(30+ lectures)** at EPIC Institute of Technology.

### Professional Experience

#### VOKI Games (Playrix)
*The #1 European mobile game publisher*

**Principal ML Engineer**
Sep 2025 – Present, Serbia, Novi Sad
*   Developed a churn prediction ML model (supervised learning) to identify at-risk players, driving an estimated **20% LTV growth**.
*   Designed and implemented a player experience embedding model based on Mamba (SSM) architecture to capture long-term behavioral patterns, reducing player segmentation mismatches by **30%**.
*   Developed a roadmap for the enterprise-wide integration of AI models, aligning ML initiatives with strategic business goals.

#### Rubbles (SBDA Group)
*Company specializing in data-driven business process optimization for large enterprises.*

**Head of Data Science & Analytics**
Jan 2023 – Aug 2025, Serbia, Novi Sad
*   Designed ML demand forecasting toolkit using supervised learning (LightGBM, XGBoost) and time series methods. Led integration into major FMCG clients (KFC, Mars, Henkel, Unilever), increasing product availability by **5%** on average.
*   Built internal LLM-based RAG system for knowledge retrieval (LangChain, FAISS). Reduced onboarding time by **50%** for new engineers.
*   Served as a primary technical liaison for the CEO and stakeholders, aligning AI roadmaps with business goals and presenting ROI-driven performance reports to C-level executives.

**Lead ML Engineer**
Apr 2022 – Jan 2023, Turkey, Istanbul
*   Engineered demand and promo elasticity models (LightGBM, XGBoost, Statsmodels) for Perfetti Van Melle, resulting in a **15% reduction in stock-outs** and a **10% decrease in excess inventory**.
*   Designed and deployed production-ready ML services using Spark and Docker, ensuring high-throughput data processing and seamless integration with backend infrastructure.
*   Orchestrated cross-functional delivery and mentored a team of 5+ developers, establishing best practices for code robustness and scalable AI infrastructure.

**Senior ML Engineer**
Nov 2021 – Apr 2022, Russian Federation, Moscow
*   Architected a global-scale demand forecasting system for a leading QSR brand, improving WAPE by **12%** through advanced feature engineering and time series modeling.
*   Directly boosted campaign ROI and product availability by implementing real-time traffic features, resulting in a **7% reduction in perishable food waste**.

#### NDA (Confidential Client)
*Largest gas producer and top oil and gas company.*

**Senior ML Engineer**
Jun 2017 – Nov 2021, Russian Federation, Moscow
*   Led the Energy Efficiency & Cost Optimization project. Developed dynamic ML models (regression, supervised learning) and factor analysis algorithms for energy consumption. Achieved an estimated **5–7% reduction in energy costs**.
*   Designed and deployed an automated anomaly detection solution for oil production (Keras, TensorFlow) on time series data. Reduced equipment downtime by **12%**.
*   Digital Twin Engineering: Architected a "Digital Twin for Oil Manufacture" MVP, simulating complex refining processes. Built the scalable backend (Python, K8s, Kafka) and interpreted ML models to identify dynamic properties of technological objects, accelerating R&D cycles for complex industrial assets.
*   Headed the Data Science department, overseeing resource allocation across multiple IIoT projects and mentoring a cross-functional team of 6+.

### Skills and Languages

*   **Languages:** Python, SQL, C++
*   **ML & Deep Learning:** PyTorch, TensorFlow, Keras, Scikit-Learn, LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, Statsmodels, Prophet, Mamba (SSM)
*   **ML Methodologies:** Time series forecasting, Anomaly detection, Supervised learning, Deep learning, Optimization, Probability, Statistics
*   **Data & MLOps:** PySpark, Databricks, Airflow, Pandas, NumPy, SciPy, Azure, Docker, Kubernetes, Kafka, MLflow
*   **Visualization & Tools:** GitLab, Jenkins, Weights & Biases (W&B), Dash, Tableau, Plotly
*   **Languages (Communication):** English — Fluent (C1)

### Education

*   **2021**: PhD Candidate in Computer Science – SPbPU (ABD)
*   **2017**: MSc in Technical Systems Management – SPbPU, Russia
*   **2015**: BSc in Computer Sciences – SPbPU, Russia
*   **2013**: Erasmus Exchange – Czech Technical University, Prague (full program in English)

### Certifications

*   **Generative AI** – DeepLearning.AI (Jan 2024)
*   **Advanced Data Science** – IBM (Jul 2023)
*   **SQL for Data Science** – UC Davis (Sep 2021)

### Additional

*   Fluent in English (Teaching and Presenting Experience).
*   Open to relocation to Germany; prepared to self-fund relocation expenses and requires only visa sponsorship.
*   [Recommendations from professionals and leaders at top-tier tech companies](https://www.linkedin.com/in/nkudriashov/details/recommendations/?detailScreenTabIndex=0)
